      "writtenOn": "2025-12-30T23:14:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It would be better to always use trim_task_dmabuf_records_locked() to avoid a situation when the process might be rescheduled onto another CPU resulting in the wrong list being trimmed. Looks like you can easily do that here. And trim_task_dmabuf_records() is used only in one other place where we can also easily avoid that. I think it would be better to post a patch that eliminates trim_task_dmabuf_records() first and then place this fix on top of it.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 768,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 768,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "3d252e64_84ac5a73",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "drivers/dma-buf/dma-buf.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 350,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 357,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": ""
            },
            {
              "path": "drivers/dma-buf/dma-buf.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 557,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 558,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "\tlocal_lock(\u0026dmabuf_rec_reloads.lock);\n\ttrim_task_dmabuf_records_locked();\n\tlocal_unlock(\u0026dmabuf_rec_reloads.lock);\n"
            },
            {
              "path": "drivers/dma-buf/dma-buf.c",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 768,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 769,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "\tlocal_lock(\u0026dmabuf_rec_reloads.lock);\n\ttrim_task_dmabuf_records_locked();\n\tlocal_unlock(\u0026dmabuf_rec_reloads.lock);\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "revId": "df95aceaa3b4c257ec727d9aecf8d4e8b936b80c",
