      "writtenOn": "2025-12-31T00:18:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That makes sense for the case where we run out of retries and `dmabuf_rec_reloads.lock` is already (still) locked. We can be sure we\u0027ll trim a list that has at least the requested number of records since we\u0027re still on the same CPU.\n\nWhat about the case where `task_dmabuf_records_preload` fails and we `goto err_prealloc`? (Same as the other case `trim_task_dmabuf_records` is called.)\nIf the preload request is for more than one record and the last allocation fails, all the earlier allocations will remain on the preload list(s) despite `task_dmabuf_records_preload` returning an error. `dmabuf_rec_reloads.lock` is unlocked in that case, so we can\u0027t know which CPU we\u0027re on or which list we\u0027ll trim. We may even end up with multiple per-cpus lists \u003e `MAX_PCP_POOL_SIZE` if count is large.",
      "parentUuid": "f6e1bf01_694996d3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 768,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 768,
        "endChar": 25
      },
      "revId": "df95aceaa3b4c257ec727d9aecf8d4e8b936b80c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
